# §Fase 124.b / D124.6 — UBSan suppressions for VENDORED code only.
#
# Vendored reference implementations are provenance-pinned (byte-identical
# to upstream; per-file SHA-256 in c-src/vendor/PROVENANCE.toml), so they
# are deliberately NOT patched to this repo's house standards — a patched
# vendor file would no longer be the artifact the provenance manifest
# attests, and correctness is held by KATs + cross-implementation interop
# instead (tests/ed25519_kat.rs, tests/mldsa_kat.rs, tests/shake_kat.rs).
#
# orlp/ed25519's constant-time table select (ge.c:359,
# `b - (((-bnegative) & b) << 1)`) left-shifts a negative signed value:
# defined behaviour in C23, UB before it, present in upstream HEAD, and
# correct on every two's-complement target. Suppressed for the vendor
# directory ONLY, and only the shift-base check — any other UB class in
# vendor code, and every check in our own kernels, still traps.
shift-base:*orlp-ed25519*
